WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:05.797
(Hudson cooing)

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.633
TORI: Wesley's being so quiet.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.093
JIM: I know. He's being so good.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:11.970
TORI: If the kids aren't crying,
things are good.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.096
JIM: Yeah.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:15.557
We got a tailwind.

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.308
It's a paddler's dream.

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.769
TORI: Yeah, just my concern
is just the wind

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:20.562
past this point, basically.

00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:22.981
JIM: I know, it's looking like
it's gonna pick up a bit.

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:25.191
A little wind is like
a gale force.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.943
What do you think about
trying something out

00:00:26.943 --> 00:00:28.570
like rigging up a sail?

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.156
TORI: Is that gonna just take
more time than just paddling?

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:32.490
JIM: If I can find
the right materials,

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.783
we could rig it up pretty quick,

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.618
and we're gonna have
to probably want to stop

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:36.953
to feed the kids anyways, right?

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:39.039
TORI: If we're stopping
for lunch, I suppose,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.665
yeah, we could try to rig it up.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:41.499
HUDSON: Ya!

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.008
JIM: (in Cockney accent)
What a nice little spot, eh?

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:51.468
Go on, guv'na!

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.136
TORI: Right into the rocks.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.512
(scrape)

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:55.597
JIM: Wee!
TORI: Boom!

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:57.140
North. Here.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.975
HUDSON: Wee!

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:00.351
JIM: Aww.

00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:02.103
TORI: Huddy, you want
some lunch?

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:04.606
JIM: Hey, hon, can I go grab
a couple sticks

00:01:04.606 --> 00:01:05.648
to rig up the sail?

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:06.524
TORI: Sure. Yeah.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:08.777
JIM: Okay. I'll be back soon.
TORI: Yup.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:12.030
JIM: If I don't come back,
never remarry.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:15.241
TORI: Did you hear that?

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:21.206
It is a little windy out there,
and so I'm sure the sail

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.875
would be a good idea if
the wind stays in our favor.

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:27.587
But if it changes, it could be
a little bit tricky.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:31.466
JIM: I'm gonna have to take
a couple small saplings.

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:33.635
So, I don't just walk into
the woods and cut down

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.845
the biggest, perfect tree
standing right in the middle.

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.013
That's a tree that's healthy

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:38.556
that's gonna live
for a long time.

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:41.101
So, they're gonna take those
from a spot

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.812
where there's a whole bunch
growing close together.

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:46.523
And that way, if I take a couple
and thin it out,

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:50.485
more trees will live
to become mature trees.

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.446
There we go. I think that'll be
just about right.

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:59.369
HUDSON: Dada!

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:00.495
JIM: I found pretty much
what I think are

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.580
the perfect things for the mast.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.124
TORI: Sweet.
JIM: Yeah.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:09.379
I am just lashing up these two
long, whippy pieces of sapling.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:12.841
That is actually going to be
the top of the mast.

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:16.261
Yeah, it's gonna be...
pretty cool!

00:02:19.013 --> 00:02:21.391
So, what I'm gonna do is I'm
gonna lash them to the gunwales

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:24.227
by wrapping a rope around
the hull of the boat.

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:26.229
And that's almost gonna
create like an arch.

00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:29.774
And then I'm gonna tie
a camping tarp to a stick.

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:31.860
Put a pulley in the top,
and that way,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.195
we can drop the sail
if it gets too windy,

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:36.698
so we'll know that we'll be
safe out there as well.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:39.408
Yeah.

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:40.535
Yeah, okay.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.911
TORI: Whoa!

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.205
Ready to set sail, honey.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.292
JIM: You know, it's a little
upsetting that Huddy's asleep,

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.169
though, and he hasn't
really soaked in

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.379
the brilliance of this sail rig.

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:53.381
He'll have to enjoy the
pictures, unless he wakes up.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:54.382
We'll see, though.

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:55.633
TORI: Ah, good boy!

00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:57.510
JIM: Okay. Okay, you ready?

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.889
TORI: Okay. Let's do it.

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.475
JIM: Alright,
I'm gonna raise it.

00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:06.853
TORI: Alright!

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.229
Ah!

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:09.898
JIM: Yeah! It's working!

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:11.399
TORI: Yeah! Woo-hoo!

00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:13.526
JIM: Woo!

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.486
TORI: This is great!
We're sailing!

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.407
JIM: Okay, cross draw.

00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:20.325
Cross draw.

00:03:20.325 --> 00:03:23.411
TORI: I am cross drawing, honey.

00:03:23.661 --> 00:03:26.706
JIM: It's working!

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.375
We could technically sail all
the way to the end of this bay

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.628
effortlessly with
the tailwind, eh?

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:33.171
TORI: I know,
I've got my feet up.

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:36.049
JIM: Just saving energy,
it's saving time.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.425
TORI: We're doing it.

00:03:37.425 --> 00:03:38.968
Too bad the kids
are both asleep.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:41.763
We should get into
sailing, honey.

00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:42.931
JIM: Yeah.

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:44.265
Bam!
TORI: Boom!

